  lines:
    '|a||How do people choose? This block asked it for thirty-odd lectures. So put its verdicts on one board: what people do, and why.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Row one, the oldest: when a price rises, people buy less of it. About as close to consensus as economics gets.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:i1e5nv'
    '|a||Row two: the option you get for doing nothing tends to stick. Make a pension opt-out instead of opt-in, and enrolment jumps. Consensus.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:igugfo'
    '|b||Row three: when a tax rebate lands, people spend a real chunk of it within months, not spread over a lifetime. Consensus again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1sobncx'
    '|a||And row four: buyers react to the first digit. Used cars sell for less just past each ten-thousand-mile mark. Mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:phrmmd'
    '|b||Row five, the newest: crowds snowball. Hits, queues, full restaurants: early choices pull later ones along. Mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kfyla7'
    '|b||Now the other column. Why do people do these things? What verdict do you think the block kept reaching?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1iezkea'
    '|b||The block''s verdict on WHY people do these things, row after row?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ck7ugo'
    '|b||Noted. The board answers row by row.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Row one: do buyers really optimise, or does a shrinking budget do the work? Contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Inertia, or a default read as advice? Contested. Impatient, or simply short of cash? Contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1yut72i'
    '|a||A clever shortcut, or a bias? Contested too. And the crowd: sound inference from what others know, or plain conformity? Contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:12jvc4x'
    '|b||So that''s the block in one pattern. What people do is mostly settled. Why they do it is where the fight is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1rvenmn'
    '|a||And the fight has four sides: rational choice, behavioural economics, Becker''s imperial reach, and norms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1yjzxm9'
    '|a||Four sides, and they all fight over the why. So where exactly do they part ways?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Start from the machine they share. Wants go in here: U, what you like, ranked best to worst. Not the same as happiness: people give up some happiness for purpose or status.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:fa8hm5'
    '|b||Prices and a budget go in here: what you can afford.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1vgxd30'
    '|b||And in the middle, the choosing: pick the best thing you can afford. That''s rational choice, whole.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:yz0kgx'
    '|a||And Becker''s imperialism? A different machine?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ejrsxt'
    '|b||Same machine, wider price box. A prison term is a price. So are a child''s hours, and the slim chance your vote counts.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:12786zw'
    '|a||Then behavioural economics rewires the middle: losses loom larger, now beats later, the default wins, and some prices go unseen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1p5p2s4'
    '|b||And norms rewrite the wants: fairness, what others expect, who you are, where you grew up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1uxnbk'
    '|a||So they''re not four theories of everything. Each keeps most of the machine and opens one box.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7q9lpq'
    '|b||Your turn. Six new cases: which box does each one poke?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ncwjc4'
    '|b||Which box does each case poke? Sort the six cards.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ldnp41'
    '|a||That''s why the four can argue at all: they share every box but one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||If each lens opens one box, when should you reach for which? Two questions sort most cases.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||First, along here: how often do you make this choice, and how fast do you learn it went wrong? Second, up here: is anyone watching?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1vl1lcp'
    '|a||Everyday and private, down here: groceries, petrol, coffee. Rational choice does well, and price changes show it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:15xsab3'
    '|b||Even sloppy shoppers help it. Becker showed that buyers who chose at random would still trace a demand curve that slopes down.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:no9pyd'
    '|a||Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:uip22a'
    '|a||Say a buyer picks a point on her budget line at random: any amount of the good from zero to I over P.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||On average she buys half the most she could: I over two P.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:122sye'
    '|a||Double the price and that average halves. A downward slope, with no optimising at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fb6rts'
    '|a||Rare and slow to pay back, over here: a pension, a gym contract. That''s where defaults and present bias bite.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1c5x5v5'
    '|b||And up top, anything others see: the tip, the fair split, the vote. Norms do much of the work there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:14uepao'
    '|b||Not everything up here is a norm, though. Joining a queue can be plain inference from what others seem to know, until it becomes a cascade.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1cbpe0f'
    '|a||A new case: choosing a mortgage, once or twice in a life. My guess is the rational corner. The stakes are huge, so people take care.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1f1r1r2'
    '|b||Where would you put it? Where does choosing a mortgage land? Tap a zone.':
